{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:05:47.144Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"420a8d8030ac0ed178789d9372657d43b7b9e0184c6a257580f344d14ac6223a","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Tobias, here are the Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers I found:\n\n• *#4409*: Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" digest (2 Jan 2026, teams/team-central/digests). There's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard, at Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake. It was open at the time of handoff.\n• *#4412*: same digest. Minor driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. Also open at handoff.\n• *#8841*: #central-random, your message on 13 Oct. West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. You flagged it for support.\n\nA caveat: none of these sources says \"Marrow Fieldworks\" next to a ticket number. The digest names Marrow Fieldworks as the account changing hands on 5 Jan, then lists #4409 and #4412 under \"Pree's dealer account.\" #8841 was raised on \"Tobias's dealer account.\" I've treated both as the same account, the dealer account that moved from Pree to you. Please check that's right before the call.\n\nI left these out because they belong to other accounts:\n• FR-882 is a Marrow *Agrisupply* feature request, not Fieldworks.\n• #4419 and #PD-4492 are Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets from Moss's North notes.\n\nMoss's Central cheat sheet and the other North digests have no Fieldworks ticket numbers."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:05:53.063Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"b31b2715b6921a5b3db37114e52f00bf06eb91f03093059f64ee0b5c336411c6","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I sent Tobias the list in your direct message. I found three ticket numbers, but none of the sources puts \"Marrow Fieldworks\" right next to a ticket number, so I asked him to check that they belong to that account before the call.\n\n- **#4409**, from Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" note (2 Jan 2026): a report keeps timing out at the Salina North yard. It was open when the account changed hands.\n- **#4412**, from the same note: a minor glitch with the text prompts drivers get. Also open when the account changed hands.\n- **#8841**, from Tobias's own message in #central-random on 13 Oct: one of the depot doors is still being double-booked, and he flagged it for support.\n\nHere is why I think they belong to Marrow Fieldworks. Moss's note names Marrow Fieldworks as the account changing hands on 5 Jan 2026. It then lists #4409 and #4412 under \"Pree's dealer account\" before that handover. In #central-random, #8841 is about \"Tobias's dealer account.\" I treated these as the same account.\n\nI left out ticket numbers from Moss's notes that belong to other accounts:\n- **FR-882** is a feature request for Marrow Agrisupply, a different account.\n- **#4419** and **#PD-4492** belong to Quarrendon Freight Lines.\n\nMoss's other notes have no Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers. Tobias is a member of #central-random, and all of Moss's notes I used are public."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
